# A throw in the send writer, the io coroutine that writes every response to
# the socket, closes that connection. The throw used to end the writer without
# closing the socket or stopping the session: the response was never sent, the
# session and the recv pump waited for the client, and the client waited for
# the response forever. The failure point removes itself when it fires, so
# only the connection that armed it loses its response.
#
# Failure points are process-global, so this lives in the recovery tree, where
# each test has a server of its own.

statement error
SET sdb_faults = 'send_writer_throw';

connection healthy
query
SELECT 1 AS ok;
----
ok
1
